  "worked_solution": "The set $C\u2216D$ is the set of all elements belonging to $C$ but *not* $D.$ Note that the elements $-1,0\\in D$ are also in $C,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C\u2216D & =C-D \\\\  & ={-3,-1,0,5,10}-{-2,-1,0,1} \\\\  & ={-3,5,10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
